---
// Big name + intro text + life story, with the dashed arrows (Figma: Bias Mode Section, top).
// Wide screens: two staggered columns and two arrows starting under the name.
// Narrow screens (≤ 900px): one column; a single arrow leads from the intro down to the life story.
// Layout changes animate gently when the window is resized.
import arrowShort from '../assets/icons/arrow-short.svg?url';
import arrowLong from '../assets/icons/arrow-long.svg?url';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { t, type Lang } from '../i18n/ui';

interface Props {
  lang: Lang;
}
const { lang } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="about container" aria-labelledby="about-name">
  <h2 id="about-name" class="title about-name">
    <span class="pii">{site.name}</span>
    <span class="pii-placeholder">{t(lang).nameHidden}</span>
  </h2>

  <div class="about-grid">
    {
      lang === 'it' ? (
        <div class="intro">
          <p>
            Sono uno UX Researcher con un debole per i videogiochi e un background in UX/UI design, il che significa che
            studio e parlo con le persone (e con i giocatori!) per capire:{' '}<u>chi</u>{' '}sono,{' '}<u>cosa</u>{' '}
            fanno,{' '}<u>perché</u>{' '}e{' '}<u>quando</u>{' '}lo fanno e{' '}<u>dove</u>{' '}agiscono.
          </p>
          <p>
            Dopo aver compreso questi punti chiave, costruisco insieme a te e ai tuoi utenti un’esperienza che li aiuti nel
            modo migliore a fare ciò che fanno, dove lo fanno: che si tratti di trovare un’aula o di non restare bloccati
            in un open world.
          </p>
        </div>
      ) : (
        <div class="intro">
          <p>
            I’m a UX Researcher with a soft spot for games and a background in UX/UI design, which means I study and
            talk with people (and players!) to understand:{' '}<u>who</u>{' '}they are,{' '}<u>what</u>{' '}they do,
            {' '}<u>why</u>{' '}and{' '}<u>when</u>{' '}they do it, and{' '}<u>where</u>{' '}they act.
          </p>
          <p>
            Having understood these key points, I craft with you and your users an experience that best helps them do
            what they do, where they do it: whether that’s finding a classroom or not getting stuck in an open world.
          </p>
        </div>
      )
    }

    <img class="arrow arrow-short" src={arrowShort} alt="" width="184" height="208" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    <img class="arrow arrow-long" src={arrowLong} alt="" width="104" height="458" loading="lazy" />
    <svg class="arrow-mobile" viewBox="-8 -6 86 212" width="86" height="212" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <path d="M14 196 C 20.6 182.2, 33.4 163.8, 40 150 C 62 104, 62 52, 44 2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="9 7" stroke-linecap="round" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" />
      <path d="M24.5 190.1 L 14 196 L 12 184.2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" />
    </svg>

    {
      lang === 'it' ? (
        <div class="life">
          <p>
            {/* hover: search "most boring city in Italy" and Rovigo comes up (from a 2014 Caterpillar / Rai Radio 2 listener poll); hidden in recruiter mode */}
            Sono cresciuto in{' '}
            <span
              class="town-tip"
              data-cursor-pii
              data-cursor="Lo sapevi? Cerca su Google “la città più noiosa d’Italia”: esce Rovigo"
              >un paese vicino a Venezia</span
            >, dove la noia mi ha spinto verso cose divertenti, come i
            videogiochi e l’informatica.
          </p>
          <p>
            Alle superiori mi sono specializzato in informatica, studiando cose divertenti come la costruzione di reti e
            tutto il resto, hardware e sistemi web… Ho anche avuto la possibilità di sviluppare applicazioni desktop e
            pagine web.
          </p>
          <p>
            Ma poi mi sono trovato davanti a un ‘grande’ dilemma: cosa fare della mia vita adesso? Una cosa che mi ha
            sempre accompagnato è l’antipatia per tutto ciò che in informatica non funziona, che non è chiaro o che
            risulta frustrante. Per questo mi sono avvicinato alla UX/UI e, più in generale, all’Interazione
            Uomo-Computer.
          </p>
          <p>
            Durante gli anni universitari ho studiato nella splendida regione del Trentino (e in <span data-cursor="uWaterloo">Canada</span> 🍁), tra montagne
            meravigliose e panorami spettacolari, imparando a costruire sistemi eccellenti. Ho appreso i metodi dell’HCI e li ho messi
            in pratica.
          </p>
          <p>Questo sono io, credo :)</p>
        </div>
      ) : (
        <div class="life">
          <p>
            I grew up in{' '}
            <span
              class="town-tip"
              data-cursor-pii
              data-cursor="Did you know? Google “Italy’s most boring city” and Rovigo comes up"
              >a town near Venice</span
            >, where boredom doomed me, so I got into fun things like video games and IT.
          </p>
          <p>
            In my high school years I got to specialise in ICT, studying fun things like building networks and all the
            other hardware and web systems stuff… I also got the chance to build desktop apps and web pages.
          </p>
          <p>
            But then I got into a ‘big’ dilemma: what should I do with my life now? Something that always stayed with
            me is the hate I have for IT stuff that doesn’t work, that is not clear, that is frustrating. That’s why I
            got into UX/UI and Human-Computer Interaction overall.
          </p>
          <p>
            So in my uni years I studied, in the beautiful Trentino region (and <span data-cursor="uWaterloo">Canada</span> 🍁), between awesome mountains and
            spectacular views, how to build great systems. I learned HCI methods and put them into practice.
          </p>
          <p>That’s me, I guess :)</p>
        </div>
      )
    }
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about {
    position: relative;
    padding-top: clamp(16px, 2vw, 28px);
    --anim: 500ms var(--ease);
  }

  .about-name {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .about-grid {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr);
    /* Figma: intro starts 242px below the top of the name at 1440px */
    margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 7vw, 6.5rem);
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    line-height: 1.3;
    transition: margin var(--anim);
  }

  .about-grid p + p {
    margin-top: 1.3em;
  }

  .intro {
    grid-column: 1 / span 7;
    grid-row: 1;
    max-width: 795px;
  }

  .life {
    grid-column: 6 / -1;
    grid-row: 3;
    max-width: 795px;
    justify-self: end;
    /* Figma: life story starts 628px below the name (just under the long arrow) */
    margin-top: clamp(4rem, 15vw, 13.5rem);
    transition: margin var(--anim), transform var(--anim);
  }

  u {
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .arrow,
  .arrow-mobile {
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
    color: var(--color-brand-ink);
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .arrow {
    position: absolute;
    transition: opacity var(--anim), transform var(--anim), left var(--anim), top var(--anim);
  }

  /* positions measured from the Figma frame (name top = 0) */
  .arrow-short {
    left: 63.6%;
    top: calc(-1 * clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5.4rem));
    width: clamp(90px, 12.8vw, 184px);
  }

  .arrow-long {
    left: 72.5%;
    top: calc(-1 * clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5.4rem));
    width: clamp(52px, 7.25vw, 104px);
  }

  /* single arrow between intro and life story, used in one-column layouts */
  .arrow-mobile {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    grid-row: 2;
    justify-self: center;
    aspect-ratio: 86 / 212;
    width: auto; /* keeps the arrow's proportions from its height */
    height: 0;
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(-12px) rotate(-6deg);
    transition: height var(--anim), opacity var(--anim), transform var(--anim), margin var(--anim);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .about-name {
      white-space: normal;
    }
    .intro,
    .life {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      justify-self: start;
    }
    .life {
      margin-top: 0;
    }
    .arrow {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(20px);
    }
    .arrow-mobile {
      height: clamp(96px, 18vw, 128px);
      margin-block: 24px 28px;
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .about-grid,
    .life,
    .arrow,
    .arrow-mobile {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
